---
import '../styles/global.css';  
---

<section class="bg-paper-dim py-[68px]">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5">
        <div class="text-center" data-anim>
          <div class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-red mb-3.5">Sound familiar?</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-[38px] font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3.5">Which of These <em class="not-italic text-red">Runs Your Firm</em> Today?</h2>
          <p class="max-w-[58ch] mx-auto mb-10 text-text-dim text-[16.5px]">Whatever you're on, the Quivr team migrates everything: clients, notes, tasks, and history, in under a week.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom p-[22px] flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-anim style="--d:0.00s">
            <h3 class="text-[17px] font-extrabold">Redtail</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">A reliable rolodex, but workflows and automation hit a ceiling as your firm grows.</p>
            <span class="self-start text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-red bg-[#F6E7E4] rounded px-2.25 py-1">Outgrown</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom p-[22px] flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-anim style="--d:0.07s">
            <h3 class="text-[17px] font-extrabold">Wealthbox</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">Easy to start, light on the operational depth a scaling advisory team needs.</p>
            <span class="self-start text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-red bg-[#F6E7E4] rounded px-2.25 py-1">Capacity Ceiling</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom p-[22px] flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-anim style="--d:0.14s">
            <h3 class="text-[17px] font-extrabold">Raw Salesforce</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">Powerful engine, endless configuration. You become the admin, or you pay one.</p>
            <span class="self-start text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-red bg-[#F6E7E4] rounded px-2.25 py-1">Consultant Trap</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom p-[22px] flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-anim style="--d:0.21s">
            <h3 class="text-[17px] font-extrabold">HubSpot</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">Built for marketing funnels, not planning workflows, compliance, or meeting cycles.</p>
            <span class="self-start text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-red bg-[#F6E7E4] rounded px-2.25 py-1">Wrong Fit</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom p-[22px] flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-anim style="--d:0.28s">
            <h3 class="text-[17px] font-extrabold">Spreadsheets / None</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">Every client detail one mis-sort away from chaos. No audit trail, no automation.</p>
            <span class="self-start text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-red bg-[#F6E7E4] rounded px-2.25 py-1">Highest Risk</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom p-[22px] flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-anim style="--d:0.35s">
            <h3 class="text-[17px] font-extrabold">Something else</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">Legacy or niche system? If your team works around it instead of in it, same problem.</p>
            <span class="self-start text-[11px] font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-red bg-[#F6E7E4] rounded px-2.25 py-1">Worth a Look</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-center font-bold mt-[26px] text-base" data-anim>Recognize yours? <em class="not-italic text-red">That's exactly what the intro call maps out: where your hours are going, and how many you'd get back.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>